---

<ProseLayout
  title="Support"
  description="Get help with MyRideSG — how to reach us, what to include, and answers to the questions riders ask most."
>
  <p>
    Something not working, or an idea for what MyRideSG should do next? Email
    <a href="mailto:hello@myridesg.com">hello@myridesg.com</a> and a human will read it.
    We aim to reply within two working days.
  </p>

  <h2>Before you write</h2>
  <p>These details get you a useful answer faster:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your phone and OS version (for example, iPhone 15 on iOS 26)</li>
    <li>What you were doing when it went wrong</li>
    <li>A screenshot, if the problem is something you can see</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please don't email us your NRIC, passwords, or card details — we will never ask for
    them.
  </p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h3>How do I delete my account?</h3>
  <p>
    In the app, go to Account → Privacy and data → Delete account. Deletion is immediate
    and cannot be undone. You do not need to contact us first.
  </p>

  <h3>Can I get my data out?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes. Account → Privacy and data → Export your data gives you a CSV of everything you
    have logged.
  </p>

  <h3>The receipt scan didn't read my receipt properly</h3>
  <p>
    Scanning fills the form in for you, but you can always correct any field before
    saving. Crumpled or faded receipts are the usual culprits. If it is consistently wrong
    for a particular workshop's receipts, send us a photo and we will look at it.
  </p>

  <h3>Why does the app ask for my location?</h3>
  <p>
    Only to show workshops near you and how far away they are, and only while the app is
    open. You can decline and still use everything else — workshop search just won't sort
    by distance.
  </p>

  <h3>A workshop's details are wrong</h3>
  <p>
    Tell us which one and what's wrong, and we will fix the listing. Rider corrections are
    how the directory stays accurate.
  </p>

  <h3>How do I stop notifications?</h3>
  <p>
    Reminders can be muted per bike in the app, and you can turn off notifications for
    MyRideSG entirely in your phone's Settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy and terms</h2>
  <p>
    Read our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and
    <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

